1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,400
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,200
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,920
This is my brother, George.
[SNORTS]

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,440
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:13,280
And this is Daddy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,520
[♪♪♪]

8
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,560
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

9
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,240
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family
are watching

10
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:27,119
their favorite television
program, Detective Potato.

11
00:00:27,119 --> 00:00:30,720
I am Detective Potato,
the world famous detective!

12
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,280
ALL:
Ooh!

13
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:34,000
Please help me,
Mr. Detective!

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,360
I cannot find
my flower anywhere!

15
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:40,160
Hm... Your flower is on
the top of your head!

16
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,199
Oh, thank you,
Mr. Detective!

17
00:00:42,199 --> 00:00:43,960
[SNORTS]
That was easy!

18
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,559
I could do that!

19
00:00:45,559 --> 00:00:48,559
Ho-ho-ho! I'm sure
you could, Peppa.

20
00:00:48,559 --> 00:00:50,239
Daddy, when I grow up,

21
00:00:50,239 --> 00:00:52,000
I want to be
a famous detective.

22
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,480
[SNORTS]

23
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,879
NARRATOR:
George wants to be
a detective too.

24
00:00:55,879 --> 00:00:57,680
If you're going to be
detectives,

25
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:02,400
you'll each need a hat.
Detectives always wear hats.

26
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,240
[SNORTS]
Now you look like
two proper detectives.

27
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,600
[SNORTS]
And we need one of

28
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,720
those funny things,

29
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,039
that makes
everything look big.

30
00:01:11,039 --> 00:01:12,880
A magnifying glass!

31
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:16,160
I think we've got one in
the kitchen drawer.

32
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,440
[SNORTS]
Here we are,

33
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:19,880
a real magnifying glass!

34
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:21,039
Wow!

35
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,640
[SNORTS]
How does it work?

36
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:26,000
You hold it in front of things
and they look bigger.

37
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,399
NARRATOR:
The magnifying glass makes
the little fish look big.

38
00:01:29,399 --> 00:01:31,839
[SNORTS]
Can I have a go?

39
00:01:31,839 --> 00:01:33,759
Wow!

40
00:01:33,759 --> 00:01:37,000
NARRATOR:
The magnifying glass makes
George's eyes look very big.

41
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,520
[GIGGLING]

42
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:43,119
Now what you detectives need,
is a mystery to solve.

43
00:01:43,119 --> 00:01:45,960
Daddy, what's
a miss-story?

44
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,479
A mystery

45
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:50,280
is something detectives
are good at sorting out.

46
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:53,199
[SNORTS]
Like finding lost things.

47
00:01:53,199 --> 00:01:56,640
I know! We can find
George's toy dinosaur!

48
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,600
[SNORTS]
That's always getting
lost.

49
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,280
Dine-Saw!

50
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,559
NARRATOR:
Mr. Dinosaur is not lost.

51
00:02:03,559 --> 00:02:04,960
Oh.
[SNORTS]

52
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,000
What about
your glasses, Daddy?

53
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,280
You're always
losing them.

54
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:13,519
Ho-ho-ho. Not today,
I'm wearing my glasses.

55
00:02:13,519 --> 00:02:15,239
It's not fair.

56
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:17,560
There aren't any
miss-stories.

57
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,799
[SNORTS]
Would you like me

58
00:02:18,799 --> 00:02:20,280
to make you a mystery?

59
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:23,560
Yes, please!
[SNORTING]

60
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,560
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig is going to make
a mystery.

61
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,840
Now.
What's on the table?

62
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:31,440
The little fish, Teddy,

63
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:34,959
a jack-in-the-box,
and Mr. Dinosaur.

64
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:36,600
[SNORTS]
That's right!

65
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,359
Now, look very hard and try
to remember them all.

66
00:02:40,359 --> 00:02:42,320
NARRATOR:
The little fish, Teddy,

67
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:45,519
a jack-in-the-box,
and Mr. Dinosaur.

68
00:02:45,519 --> 00:02:47,120
Have you
remembered them?

69
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,720
Yes.
[SNORTS]

70
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:52,440
Okay. You just have to go
outside for a moment.

71
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,720
I'll call you
when I'm ready.

72
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:56,840
[DOOR SLAMS SHUT, FOOTSTEPS]

73
00:02:56,840 --> 00:03:02,200
PEPPA:
It sounds like Daddy
is going upstairs...

74
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:05,040
And now he is
coming down again.

75
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:07,799
All right, you can
come back inside now.

76
00:03:07,799 --> 00:03:09,079
[GIGGLES]

77
00:03:09,079 --> 00:03:10,920
One thing is missing
from the table.

78
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:13,040
[SNORTS]
Do you know what?

79
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:16,320
Mr. Dinosaur is there...
little fish...

80
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,679
jack-in-the-box...

81
00:03:17,679 --> 00:03:19,640
So who's missing?

82
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,840
Um... Teddy!

83
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:24,280
That's right!
Teddy's gone!

84
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,679
Well done,
Peppa and George!

85
00:03:26,679 --> 00:03:28,720
It was quite easy
for us.

86
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,880
We are
famous detectives.

87
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,880
Ah. But that's only
half the mystery.

88
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,480
Where has Teddy gone?

89
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:37,640
Oh. I don't know.

90
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:40,720
What are those little
things on the floor?

91
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,600
They're cake crumbs.

92
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:46,399
NARRATOR:
The magnifying glass makes
the cake crumbs easy to see.

93
00:03:46,399 --> 00:03:49,920
[SNORTS]
I wonder if Teddy
has been eating cake.

94
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,840
And the crumbs
lead this way.

95
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:56,200
[SNORTS]
Teddy's been eating
a lot of cake.

96
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:59,799
NARRATOR:
The crumbs lead into Peppa
and George's bedroom.

97
00:03:59,799 --> 00:04:01,920
Oh.
The crumbs have stopped.

98
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:04,320
[SNORTS]
How can we find Teddy?

99
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,000
Ask me some questions.

100
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,320
But I will only answer
yes or no.

101
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:13,440
Okay. Um...
Is Teddy in this room?

102
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,560
Yes.

103
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:17,760
Is Teddy in George's bed?
No.

104
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:22,760
Is Teddy... somewhere high up?
Yes.

105
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,400
Teddy's in my bed!

106
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,560
ALL:
Hooray!

107
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,240
NARRATOR:
The mystery is solved.

108
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,520
[BOTH GIGGLE]

109
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:31,159
Ho, ho! Do you still
want to be a detective

110
00:04:31,159 --> 00:04:32,599
when you grow up, Peppa?

111
00:04:32,599 --> 00:04:35,360
Being a detective
is quite hard.

112
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,800
[SNORTS]
Next time,

113
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:39,560
I want to be the one
who makes the mysteries,

114
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:42,599
like you did, Daddy.

115
00:04:42,599 --> 00:04:45,880
[ALL LAUGH]

116
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,760
[CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY]

117
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,479
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

118
00:04:52,479 --> 00:04:55,960
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends
are at the playground.

119
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:59,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa, Suzy and Danny
are on the roundabout.

120
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,599
[SNORTS]
Are you all ready?

121
00:05:00,599 --> 00:05:02,000
KIDS:
Ready!

122
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,719
Then let's go!
[SNORTS]

123
00:05:04,719 --> 00:05:09,120
Whee! Faster! Faster!
Ho, ho.

124
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:13,479
Whee! Ha-ha-ha!

125
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:16,479
NARRATOR:
George is a bit too little
for the roundabout.

126
00:05:16,479 --> 00:05:19,919
He is playing on the swing. 
[SNORTS]

127
00:05:19,919 --> 00:05:21,640
[♪♪♪]

128
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:23,120
NARRATOR:
Here is Rebecca Rabbit,

129
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,960
with her little brother,
Richard Rabbit.

130
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,640
[SQUEAKS]
Hello, everyone!

131
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,479
[SQUEAKS]

132
00:05:29,479 --> 00:05:31,520
ALL: Hello!
SUZY: Baaa!

133
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:33,840
Can I come on
the roundabout too?

134
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,120
[SNORTS]
Hop on, Rebecca!

135
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:38,599
[GIGGLES]
Let's go really, really, fast!

136
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:40,440
[SQUEAKS]

137
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,200
NARRATOR:
Richard Rabbit wants to go
on the roundabout too.

138
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:48,680
Oh. If Richard gets on,
it means we can't go fast.

139
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:51,039
Richard can play
with George.

140
00:05:51,039 --> 00:05:54,240
Richard, would you like
to play with George?

141
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,520
No!

142
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:58,359
George has a dinosaur,
just like yours.

143
00:05:58,359 --> 00:06:00,719
Let's go and see.

144
00:06:00,719 --> 00:06:03,359
NARRATOR:
Richard Rabbit
is the same age as George.

145
00:06:03,359 --> 00:06:05,760
Richard wanted to see
George's dinosaur.

146
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:08,280
Grrr! Dine-Saw!

147
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,440
[BOTH GIGGLING]

148
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,599
[SNORTS]
George, can Richard

149
00:06:11,599 --> 00:06:13,200
play with
your dinosaur?

150
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,800
No!

151
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:17,400
Richard, can George
play with your dinosaur?

152
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,280
No!

153
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:22,479
NARRATOR:
George and Richard do not want
to share their dinosaurs.

154
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:27,080
[SNORTS]
George, it will be much
more fun if you share.

155
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,599
That was really nice
of George.

156
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:33,320
[LAUGHS]
Dinosaur!

157
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,320
[SOBS]

158
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,240
NARRATOR:
George does not like sharing.

159
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,960
Richard, let George
hold the dinosaurs now.

160
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,320
[GIGGLES]
[CRIES]

161
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:45,680
NARRATOR:
Richard does not like
sharing either.

162
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,280
[BOTH CRYING]

163
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,599
What's all this
crying about?

164
00:06:49,599 --> 00:06:53,640
George and Richard always cry
when they play together.

165
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:56,760
They're just too little
to play properly.

166
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:59,479
Can you two big girls
teach them to play together?

167
00:06:59,479 --> 00:07:00,760
Of course.

168
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:03,320
We can help them
make sand castles.

169
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:05,760
Good idea! Let's go
to the sandpit!

170
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:08,000
[SNORTS]
[SQUEAKS]

171
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,719
[♪♪♪]

172
00:07:09,719 --> 00:07:11,680
[GIGGLING]
NARRATOR: George and Richard

173
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,919
love the sandpit!

174
00:07:12,919 --> 00:07:15,039
[SNORTS]
George. Richard.

175
00:07:15,039 --> 00:07:19,080
Today we are going
to make sand castles.

176
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:22,159
First, we fill the buckets
with sand.

177
00:07:24,719 --> 00:07:29,280
We turn the buckets over,
and give them a little tap.

178
00:07:31,479 --> 00:07:33,960
Now, we lift the buckets!

179
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,599
And presto!

180
00:07:35,599 --> 00:07:37,799
NARRATOR:
Richard has made
a sand castle.

181
00:07:37,799 --> 00:07:39,359
Hey, presto.

182
00:07:39,359 --> 00:07:41,440
NARRATOR:
And George has made
a sand castle.

183
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:43,320
[SNORTS]
[SQUEAKS]

184
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:45,159
[BOTH GIGGLE]
DADDY PIG: You see,

185
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:48,039
[SNORTS]
playing together
is fun.

186
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:52,159
[CRIES]

187
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:54,719
[CRIES]

188
00:07:54,719 --> 00:07:55,799
[BOTH SOBBING]

189
00:07:55,799 --> 00:07:57,120
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.

190
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:59,080
This game has not gone
very well.

191
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,320
It was your brother's
fault.

192
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:04,719
[SNORTS]
He broke George's
sand castle.

193
00:08:04,719 --> 00:08:06,520
[SQUEAKS]
Your brother

194
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,359
broke my brother's
sand castle first.

195
00:08:09,359 --> 00:08:10,640
DADDY PIG:
Now, now!

196
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,840
You two big girls
are meant to be teaching

197
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:15,599
Richard and George
to play nicely together.

198
00:08:15,599 --> 00:08:18,120
That's right.
We're big girls.

199
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:20,359
And George and Richard
are too little

200
00:08:20,359 --> 00:08:22,280
to play together
properly.

201
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:24,159
Hm.
I've got an idea.

202
00:08:24,159 --> 00:08:25,799
[SNORTS]
George?

203
00:08:25,799 --> 00:08:28,760
What's your most favorite thing
in the whole playground?

204
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,039
[SNORTS]
Seesaw!

205
00:08:31,039 --> 00:08:32,959
NARRATOR:
George loves the seesaw.

206
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:36,679
[LAUGHING]

207
00:08:36,679 --> 00:08:39,319
Seesaw!
[SEESAW SQUEAKS]

208
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:42,600
NARRATOR:
It is a bit difficult to play
on a seesaw on your own.

209
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,799
[WHIMPERING]

210
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:45,360
[SQUEAKS]

211
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,600
NARRATOR:
Richard wants to play
on the seesaw.

212
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,760
[GIGGLES]

213
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,560
Seesaw!
Seesaw!

214
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,120
Seesaw!

215
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:56,439
Look! George and Richard
are playing together.

216
00:08:56,439 --> 00:08:59,400
Seesaw!
Seesaw!

217
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,800
Seesaw!
Seesaw!

218
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,959
[GIGGLING]

219
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,520
NARRATOR:
George likes Richard.

220
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,079
[SQUEAKING, GIGGLES]

221
00:09:06,079 --> 00:09:08,319
NARRATOR:
Richard likes George.

222
00:09:08,319 --> 00:09:10,880
NARRATOR:
George and Richard
like playing together.

223
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,439
[ALL LAUGHING]

224
00:09:12,439 --> 00:09:15,600
♪ Seesaw seesaw ♪

225
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,880
[SNORTING]

226
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,959
[♪♪♪]

227
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,240
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

228
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,839
[HORN HONKS]

229
00:09:25,839 --> 00:09:27,760
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George
are playing

230
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,079
at Granny and Grandpa Pig's
house today.

231
00:09:30,079 --> 00:09:33,120
[BOTH LAUGHING]

232
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,040
[SNORTS]
Hello, Grandpa Pig!

233
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,160
Baba Ig!

234
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:40,240
Ho! ho! Hello, Peppa.
Hello, George.

235
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,959
[SNORTS]
Grandpa, what
are you doing?

236
00:09:42,959 --> 00:09:45,199
I'm making
a flower garden.

237
00:09:45,199 --> 00:09:46,640
BOTH:
Ooh.

238
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:50,520
These seeds will grow into
beautiful flowers.

239
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:55,120
[SNORTS]
I drop the seeds
on the ground.

240
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:58,240
Then I cover the seeds
with earth.

241
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,360
Oh! Where have they gone?

242
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,240
NARRATOR:
The seeds have disappeared.

243
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:06,199
That's strange, I'm sure
I put some seeds here.

244
00:10:06,199 --> 00:10:09,160
Yes, Grandpa, we saw you.
[SNORTS]

245
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,720
Well they're not here now.

246
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,959
[SNORTS]
Oh, well,

247
00:10:11,959 --> 00:10:14,160
I'll just have to use
some more.

248
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:19,400
As I was saying, I simply drop
the seeds on the ground.

249
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:25,040
NARRATOR:
A little bird is eating
Grandpa Pig's flower seeds.

250
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,240
Oi! Get off my seeds!
[TWEETING]

251
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,760
So that's where
all my seeds went!

252
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:34,880
Into the little bird's tummy!
[BOTH GIGGLE]

253
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:38,160
NARRATOR:
Two more little birds are
eating Grandpa Pig's seeds.

254
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,640
Oh! Look!

255
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:42,000
Ah! Shoo! Shoo!
[CHIRPING]

256
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,240
[SNORTS]
What's all this noise?

257
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:48,240
Granny Pig, the birds are
eating all my flower seeds.

258
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,600
So we're chasing
the birds away!

259
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,520
[SNORTS]
There's no point
chasing them.

260
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,800
They'll just
come back again. Look!

261
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:58,040
We need a scarecrow.

262
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,959
What's a scarecrow?

263
00:10:59,959 --> 00:11:03,800
A scarecrow is a straw man
that scares birds away.

264
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:06,360
What a good idea,
Granny Pig.

265
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,240
[SNORTS]
I'll make one.

266
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:11,280
Come on, everyone.

267
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,880
Bye-bye, little birds,

268
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:15,400
we're going to make
a scarecrow.

269
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,920
[CHIRPING]

270
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:20,360
NARRATOR:
This is Grandpa Pig's
garden shed.

271
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:24,040
There'll be plenty of things
in here to make a scarecrow.

272
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:26,719
[SNORTS]
First, we need two sticks,

273
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:28,120
and some string.

274
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,079
We'll find them.
[SNORTS]

275
00:11:30,079 --> 00:11:32,400
[GIGGLING]

276
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,079
NARRATOR:
Peppa has found some sticks.

277
00:11:34,079 --> 00:11:35,880
George has found
some string.

278
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:40,839
Good! I'll tie the sticks
together to make the body.

279
00:11:40,839 --> 00:11:43,880
NARRATOR:
Granny Pig has found some
straw and an old sack.

280
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:48,640
Lovely! I'll put the straw
in the sack to make the head.

281
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,920
[BOTH LAUGH]

282
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:52,680
Now the scarecrow needs
something to wear.

283
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:55,079
Here's a bag of old clothes.

284
00:11:55,079 --> 00:11:56,760
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Ooh!

285
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:00,319
NARRATOR:
George has found a dress.

286
00:12:00,319 --> 00:12:02,040
[SNORTS]
[GIGGLES]

287
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,480
Silly George!

288
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:07,199
Mr. Scarecrow doesn't want
to wear a dress.

289
00:12:07,199 --> 00:12:08,360
[BOTH GIGGLE]

290
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa has found a coat.

291
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,800
Very good, Peppa.

292
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:14,800
[SNORTS]

293
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,319
NARRATOR:
George has found a hat.

294
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:18,280
Very good, George.

295
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,079
Mr. Scarecrow
needs a face.

296
00:12:21,079 --> 00:12:25,079
That's right. Would you and
George like to paint a face?

297
00:12:25,079 --> 00:12:26,400
Yes, please.

298
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:27,880
[LAUGHING]

299
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:31,280
NARRATOR:
George paints
the eyes and nose.

300
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,040
Peppa paints the mouth.

301
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:35,199
Fantastic!

302
00:12:35,199 --> 00:12:36,959
NARRATOR:
Mr. Scarecrow is ready.

303
00:12:36,959 --> 00:12:38,360
ALL:
Hooray!

304
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,360
[MUNCHING]

305
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:43,560
NARRATOR:
The little birds are looking
for Grandpa Pig's flower seeds.

306
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,839
Look! The little birds
are back.

307
00:12:45,839 --> 00:12:47,000
Don't worry, Peppa.

308
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,760
Mr. Scarecrow
will scare them off.

309
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,240
[TWEETING]

310
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:58,920
NARRATOR:
It worked. Mr. Scarecrow has
scared the little birds away.

311
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:00,120
ALL:
Hooray!

312
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,560
[SNORTS]
Good.

313
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:04,079
Now my flower seeds
will not be eaten.

314
00:13:04,079 --> 00:13:06,319
[TWEETING]

315
00:13:06,319 --> 00:13:10,040
Oh, Grandpa.
The birds look very sad.

316
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:12,680
Yes, they must
be hungry.

317
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,680
That's why
I've brought this.

318
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,640
What's that, Granny?

319
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,120
It's a bird feeder.

320
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:21,439
[SNORTS]
Grandpa, may I have
some seeds, please?

321
00:13:24,319 --> 00:13:25,719
[TWEETING]

322
00:13:25,719 --> 00:13:28,520
Come on, birdies,
lunchtime.

323
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,480
[MUNCHING]

324
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,520
Now the birdies have
their own seeds to eat.

325
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:35,800
Hooray! The little birds
are happy again. Hee-hee!

326
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:38,480
NARRATOR:
Peppa is glad
that Grandpa Pig's seeds

327
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,680
will not be eaten.

328
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,240
But she is even more glad

329
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,760
that the little birds
will not be hungry.

330
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:46,599
[ALL LAUGHING]

331
00:13:46,599 --> 00:13:47,880
[SNORTING]

332
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,959
[♪♪♪]

333
00:13:52,079 --> 00:13:54,839
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

334
00:13:54,839 --> 00:13:57,000
NARRATOR:
Today, Peppa is going
to the park.

335
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,240
ALL:
Brrr!

336
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,439
It's freezing
cold!

337
00:14:00,439 --> 00:14:02,400
It is cold!
Brrr!

338
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,280
Quick! Let's get
our warm clothes on.

339
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:06,680
[♪♪♪]

340
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,959
NARRATOR:
On cold days,
Peppa and her family

341
00:14:08,959 --> 00:14:11,560
wear their hats
and scarves and coats.

342
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,439
I'll put the roof up.
[SNORTS]

343
00:14:13,439 --> 00:14:14,920
Ooh, and let's get
the heating on.

344
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,599
[HEATER WHOOSHING]

345
00:14:16,599 --> 00:14:18,079
Everyone nice and warm?

346
00:14:18,079 --> 00:14:19,599
FAMILY:
Yes, Daddy Pig!

347
00:14:19,599 --> 00:14:22,120
[SNORTS]
Then let's go!

348
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:24,640
[HORN HONKS]

349
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,680
NARRATOR: This is the park.
[HORN HONKS]

350
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,560
[SNORTS]
We're here!

351
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:31,599
ALL: Hooray!
[KIDS GIGGLING]

352
00:14:31,599 --> 00:14:33,880
[SNORTS]
Mommy, why are all the leaves

353
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,280
red and yellow?

354
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:37,360
It's autumn time,
Peppa.

355
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,640
NARRATOR:
In the autumn,
it gets a bit colder,

356
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,800
and the leaves change color.

357
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,800
[WIND WHISTLING]

358
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,880
Brrr! It's quite windy.

359
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:48,160
Let's play a game
to keep warm.

360
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,199
[KIDS GIGGLING]

361
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,959
[SNORTS]
My turn!

362
00:14:54,959 --> 00:14:57,839
Oh. It's not meant
to go that way.

363
00:14:57,839 --> 00:15:00,760
NARRATOR:
The wind is blowing
the ball along.

364
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:04,240
[QUACKING]

365
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,599
[SNORTS]
The ball is in
the pond.

366
00:15:06,599 --> 00:15:09,719
Hm. I'll just use
this stick to reach it.

367
00:15:09,719 --> 00:15:11,040
[♪♪♪]

368
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,959
Just a bit further,
Daddy.

369
00:15:12,959 --> 00:15:15,120
[SNORTS]
Be careful, Daddy Pig...

370
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,760
[SNORTS]
Don't worry.

371
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,640
I've almost got it.

372
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:20,000
Whoa!

373
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,599
[LAUGHING]
[QUACKING]

374
00:15:21,599 --> 00:15:24,400
Daddy, is
the water cold?

375
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:27,599
A little bit. Brrr.
[WIND WHISTLING]

376
00:15:27,599 --> 00:15:30,160
NARRATOR:
The wind has blown
the ball out of the pond.

377
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:31,760
[SNORTS]
That's lucky.

378
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:34,880
Yes.
What a stroke of luck.

379
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:37,520
MOMMY PIG:
It's getting even windier.

380
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:40,760
[SNORTS]
Hold onto your hats.

381
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:44,079
NARRATOR:
Oh, no! The wind has blown
George's hat off!

382
00:15:44,079 --> 00:15:45,680
[CRYING]

383
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:49,040
Don't worry George,
Daddy Pig will catch your hat!

384
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,640
Quick, Daddy!
[SNORTS]

385
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:53,880
[WIND CONTINUES WHISTLING]

386
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,439
[PANTING]

387
00:15:57,319 --> 00:15:58,520
PEPPA: Look!
[SNORTS]

388
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,479
It's in
that little tree!

389
00:16:00,479 --> 00:16:03,479
Hm. I'll just
climb up and get it.

390
00:16:03,479 --> 00:16:05,439
[SNORTS]
The tree's much too thin

391
00:16:05,439 --> 00:16:07,280
to take your weight,
Daddy Pig.

392
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:10,719
So how can we get
George's hat?
Simple.

393
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,959
I'll give the tree
a little shake.

394
00:16:12,959 --> 00:16:16,040
[LEAVES RUSTLING]

395
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:19,040
Hm. Maybe if I shake it
a bit harder...

396
00:16:20,079 --> 00:16:23,599
Oh!
[ALL GASP]

397
00:16:23,599 --> 00:16:25,959
[SPUTTERING]
[FAMILY GIGGLING]

398
00:16:25,959 --> 00:16:28,680
I thought that sort of thing
only happened to me!

399
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,479
[SNORTS]
It's not funny.

400
00:16:30,479 --> 00:16:32,760
It is a bit funny,
Mommy.

401
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:34,839
I suppose
it is a bit funny.

402
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:37,319
[ALL LAUGH]

403
00:16:37,319 --> 00:16:38,560
Where's George's hat?

404
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,760
[SNORTS]
It's on your head.

405
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:43,120
Ha, ha!
Here's your hat, George.

406
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,959
Hold onto it this time.
[WIND WHISTLING]

407
00:16:44,959 --> 00:16:46,760
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

408
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:50,719
NARRATOR:
The wind is blowing all
the leaves off the trees.

409
00:16:50,719 --> 00:16:54,839
Look at me! I'm leaning
into the wind! Ha, ha!

410
00:16:54,839 --> 00:16:57,640
NARRATOR:
The wind is strong enough
to hold Peppa up.

411
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,359
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES]

412
00:16:59,359 --> 00:17:01,959
NARRATOR:
The wind is strong enough
to hold George up.

413
00:17:01,959 --> 00:17:04,280
[SNORTS]
Daddy! Have a go!

414
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:06,399
Uh, I'm a bit too heavy.

415
00:17:06,399 --> 00:17:09,560
Come on, Daddy!
It's really fun!

416
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:11,440
Oh, all right.

417
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:14,879
NARRATOR:
The wind is strong enough
to hold up Daddy Pig.

418
00:17:14,879 --> 00:17:16,839
Hee-hee-hee-hee! I say!

419
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:18,399
This is fun!
[SNORTS]

420
00:17:18,399 --> 00:17:21,240
Come on, Mommy Pig!
Give it a try!

421
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:24,040
But if the wind stops,
I'll fall over.

422
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:28,240
Ho, ho!
The wind won't just stop!

423
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:29,840
NARRATOR:
The wind has stopped.

424
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,520
Ooh.
Ooh.
Ooh.

425
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,280
Hee-hee-hee-hee!

426
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,879
[SNORTS]
It's not funny.

427
00:17:34,879 --> 00:17:37,040
It is a bit funny!

428
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:39,240
[ALL LAUGH]

429
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,320
[SNORTS]
Now the wind has stopped,

430
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:43,240
what can we do?

431
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,960
Hm. What's your favorite game?

432
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:49,360
Jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

433
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,919
But there aren't
any puddles.

434
00:17:51,919 --> 00:17:54,919
Just lots of boring,
dry leaves.

435
00:17:54,919 --> 00:17:57,639
And what do you do
with dry leaves?

436
00:17:57,639 --> 00:17:59,440
[SNORTS]
I don't know.

437
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,040
Jump up and down
in them!

438
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:05,399
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig loves jumping up
and down in leaves.

439
00:18:05,399 --> 00:18:08,320
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves jumping up
and down in leaves.

440
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:10,480
Everyone loves
jumping up and down in leaves.

441
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,639
[ALL LAUGHING]

442
00:18:11,639 --> 00:18:15,399
This is
the best autumn day ever.

443
00:18:15,399 --> 00:18:18,879
[ALL LAUGHING]

444
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:21,120
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

445
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,879
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

446
00:18:22,879 --> 00:18:24,879
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

447
00:18:24,879 --> 00:18:25,879
[SNORTS]

448
00:18:25,879 --> 00:18:27,600
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

449
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:29,919
[SNORTS, LAUGHS]

450
00:18:29,919 --> 00:18:31,879
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

451
00:18:31,879 --> 00:18:33,720
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

